## 3. PASS 2: Critical Self-Review & Verification (Second Run)

### Verification of Pass 1 Assumptions & Blind Spot Analysis

| Potential Blind Spot | Verification Result | Architectural Impact |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Are all 31 package manifests covered by `grammar.asn`?** | **NO.** Only 18 registries exist. 12 packages in `asl/packages/` and `browser-plugin` have no `grammar.asn`. | **High**: Gate 6 does not fail them; it simply ignores them. 441 exported symbols are unmonitored by CI. |
| **Does Gate 2 guarantee true AST syntactic balance?** | **NO.** Gate 2 uses `openP === closeP`, not a stack parser. | **Medium**: [`harness/src/ablation.asl`](file:///Users/purplelephant/projects/asex/harness/src/ablation.asl#L76-L86) contained a crossed `(let [ ... ) ]` delimiter error that was masked. |
| **Does Gate 4 truly scan 100% of non-build code?** | **PARTIAL.** Gate 4 explicitly ignores folders named `benchmarks`. | **Low**: [`harness/benchmarks/runners/eval-models.mjs`](file:///Users/purplelephant/projects/asex/harness/benchmarks/runners/eval-models.mjs) exists without tripping Gate 4. |
| **Are there single-letter abbreviations in ungrammared packages?** | **NO.** An independent scan of the 441 ungrammared symbols found 0 occurrences of `st` or `t`. | **Low**: The naming standards were adhered to by developers even without the active registry file. |

